## 2. GGUF Split: Reject Non-Contiguous Shard Numbers

**Component:** `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — `gguf_split_paths()`

**Responsibilities:** Resolves any shard path of a split model into the ordered list of all shard paths, verifying each exists on disk.

**Problem:** The function rewrites only the five-digit shard number and checks existence, but does not verify that the parsed `no` (the shard number in the given path) is consistent with the file actually being one of the shards. A file named `model-00003-of-00005.gguf` that is actually a copy of shard 1 passes silently. More critically, if a user passes a path whose digits parse to `no=0` or `no>n`, the function returns `{any}` (treating it as a single-shard model) rather than reporting the malformed name.

**Proposed change:** When the name matches the split pattern but `no` is out of range, throw rather than silently treating it as a single file.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ -38,7 +38,10 @@ inline std::vector<std::string> gguf_split_paths(const std::string& any) {
         no = no * 10 + (a - '0');
         n = n * 10 + (b - '0');
     }
-    if (n < 1 || no < 1 || no > n) return {any};
+    if (n < 1) return {any};
+    if (no < 1 || no > n)
+        throw std::runtime_error("GGUF: '" + any + "' names shard " + std::to_string(no) +
+                                 " of " + std::to_string(n) + ", which is out of range");
     std::vector<std::string> out;
     for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {
         char num[8];
```

**Verification cases:**
1. **Out-of-range shard:** Pass `model-00007-of-00005.gguf`. Must throw with a message naming the file and showing 7 > 5.
2. **Zero shard:** Pass `model-00000-of-00005.gguf`. Must throw rather than returning a single-element vector.

