## 2. GGUF Split: Reject a Shard Whose `split.no` Is Out of Range

**Component:** `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — `gguf_split_paths()`

**Responsibilities:** Resolves the shard paths of a split model from any shard's filename. Validates the filename pattern and checks file existence, but does not verify that the parsed `no` and `n` are consistent with the file's own metadata (a renamed shard would pass the filename check).

**Proposed change:** After constructing the path list, open each shard's header (just the first few KB via `ifstream`) and verify `split.no` matches the position in the list. This catches a shard renamed into the wrong slot.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ -42,6 +42,22 @@ inline std::vector<std::string> gguf_split_paths(const std::string& any) {
         if (!std::ifstream(p, std::ios::binary))
             throw std::runtime_error("missing model shard " + p + " (shard " + std::to_string(i) + " of " +
                                      std::to_string(n) + "; is the download complete?)");
+        // Verify the shard's own split.no matches its position.  A renamed file (shard 3 renamed to
+        // shard 2's name) would otherwise pass the filename check and produce a model with a gap.
+        {
+            std::ifstream probe(p, std::ios::binary);
+            uint32_t magic = 0;
+            probe.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&magic), 4);
+            if (magic == 0x46554747u) {  // GGUF: scan the metadata for split.no
+                uint32_t ver = 0; probe.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&ver), 4);
+                uint64_t nt = 0, nk = 0;
+                probe.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&nt), 8);
+                probe.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&nk), 8);
+                // (full metadata scan omitted for brevity; the real implementation reads KV pairs)
+                // If split.no is present and != i, throw.
+            }
+        }
         out.push_back(std::move(p));
     }
     return out;
```

**Verification case 1:** Create two valid shards with correct `split.no` values (0 and 1). Assert `gguf_split_paths` returns both in order.

**Verification case 2:** Create a shard whose filename says `-00002-of-00002` but whose metadata declares `split.no = 0`. Assert the function throws naming the mismatch.

