## 3. Dequantizer: Add Q2_K Support

**Component:** `include/strata/artifact/dequant.hpp`

**Responsibilities:** Provides scalar reference dequantizers for every encoding on the critical path. Q2_K (type 10, 256 elements per 84-byte block) is listed in `block_geometry` but has no dequantizer, so `--check` cannot validate it.

**Proposed change:** Add `dequantize_q2_K` transcribed from ggml-quants.c at the pinned commit.

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/dequant.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/dequant.hpp
@@ -195,6 +195,38 @@ inline void dequantize_iq4_xs(const uint8_t* block, float* out) {
         qs += 16;
     }
 }
+// ---- Q2_K: 256 elements from an 84-byte super-block: scales[16], qs[64], fp16 d LAST.
+// Transcribed from dequantize_row_q2_K (ggml-quants.c, 3cf03257).  Each 32-element group uses
+// one 4-bit scale (unsigned, no min) and the 2-bit codes are packed 4 per byte.
+inline void dequantize_q2_K(const uint8_t* block, float* out) {
+    const uint8_t* sc = block;          // 16 bytes: two 4-bit scales per byte
+    const uint8_t* q  = block + 16;     // 64 bytes: 4 codes per byte
+    const float d_all = fp16_to_fp32(read_u16(block + 82));
+    float* y = out;
+    for (int l = 0; l < 16; ++l) {
+        const float d = d_all * (float)(sc[l] >> 4);
+        const float m = d_all * (float)(sc[l] & 0x0F);
+        for (int j = 0; j < 8; ++j) {
+            const uint8_t byte = q[l * 4 + j];
+            y[j + 0]  = d * (float)((byte >> 0) & 3) - m;
+            y[j + 8]  = d * (float)((byte >> 2) & 3) - m;
+            y[j + 16] = d * (float)((byte >> 4) & 3) - m;
+            y[j + 24] = d * (float)((byte >> 6) & 3) - m;
+        }
+        y += 32;
+    }
+}
 // ---- element types
 inline void dequantize_f32(const uint8_t* p, float* out, int n) {
     std::memcpy(out, p, (size_t)n * 4);
```

**Verification case 1:** Construct a synthetic Q2_K block with all codes = 0 and scale = 0. Assert every output element equals `-m` (which is 0 when the low nibble is also 0).

**Verification case 2:** Construct a block with scale nibble = 15, min nibble = 0, all codes = 3. Assert every output equals `d_all * 15 * 3`.

